/target
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
# A west workspace assembled around this repo. Since the split, west puts
# zephyr/, modules/ and bootloader/ BESIDE this repository (ws/boards/ is the
# manifest repo), so these entries only guard against someone initialising a
# workspace inside the checkout by mistake.
#
# /zephyr/ is NOT in this list any more, and that absence is load-bearing:
# zephyr/module.yml is a tracked file -- it is what makes this repository a
# Zephyr module with board_root, which is what makes the out-of-tree board
# variants exist. The old entry silently ate that file out of `git add -A`, and
# the result was CI failing with "board qualifiers not found" on a variant that
# built perfectly in every local workspace, because the local sync did not
# respect gitignore. An ignore rule named after a directory that can no longer
# legitimately appear is not safe, it is a trap.
/.west/
/modules/
/bootloader/
/tools/
# West/CMake build trees. The glob matters: naming individual trees is how
# build-diag/, build-pico-idle/, build-pico-novalidate/ and build-pico-recovery/
# were committed by accident -- 6300 files of build output.
/build/
/build-*/
/firmware/**/build/
# generated provisioning artefacts
provision.uf2
provision.hex
# local artefacts
*.bin
*.hex
*.elf
/flash.bin
# ...but the signed test fixtures are source, not artefacts: the e2e tests
# include_bytes! them, so without these a fresh clone does not COMPILE.
# Signed image fixtures ARE tracked: the tests include_bytes! them, so a clone
# without them cannot compile. Keep this path in step with the crate name -- it
# said `smp-client` after the rename to `runtt-smp`, which quietly re-broke the
# thing it exists to prevent.
!crates/runtt-smp/tests/fixtures/*.bin

# Local-only: host setup notes specific to one machine (paths, USB topology,
# group membership). Useful to have to hand, not useful to anyone else, and not
# something to publish.
/docs/PREREQUISITES.md

# Board flash backups stay LOCAL. The blobs contain a vendor bootloader and are
# specific to one physical board, and BACKUP.sha256 only verifies files that live
# next to it -- so in a clone it checksums nothing. Keep the backup on the machine
# that holds the board; scripts/flash-feather.sh finds it beside or above the repo.
/feather-backup/
/nrf52840-backup-*/
